0,"Chatino, Zenzontepec | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/czn/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..gVDXI07EuI67QrJW-eVjyIgIpUV3R-vJBCV4FrVwf1g,Zenzontepec Chatino is a stable indigenous language of Mexico. It belongs to the Otomanguean language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,"Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
1,Episode 39: Eric W. Campbell on Otomanguean Language...,https://fieldnotespod.com/episode-39-eric-w-campbell-on-otomanguean-language-documentation-mobilization/,"So, the Otomanguean language present an example of lexical tone with many different contrasts both in terms of what are the tonal elements in the language and then the tonal melodies that you find on words which then are very much a part of the morphology of the language.","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
2,(PDF) Tone and inflection in Zenzontepec Chatino (2016),https://www.academia.edu/31055939/Tone_and_inflection_in_Zenzontepec_Chatino_2016_,"Tone in Zenzontepec Chatino is crucial for distinguishing person and aspect/mood inflection. Person inflection uses predictable tonal changes, while aspect/mood inflection involves unpredictable, lexically specified tone patterns.","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
3,Twentieth Century Sound Change in Zenzontepec,https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ec41a332c820e196d4ea9d6/t/5ede70353e270a4fa13536fe/1591636021304/paper.pdf,The Chatino languages are a shallow family of four attested languages (Boas 1913; Campbell 2013; Sullivant In press) that are coordinate with the Zapotec languages in the Zapotecan branch of Otomanguean (Mechling 1912; Kaufman 2006).,"Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
4,Chatino Zenzontepec(@chatinozenzontepec) | TikTok,https://www.tiktok.com/@chatinozenzontepec,TikTok for Good Advertise Sell on TikTok Shop TikTok LIVE Creator Networks Developers Transparency TikTok Embeds SoundOn Music Distribution TikTok Live. Terms & Policies. Chatino Zenzontepec. Seguir. Mensaje.,"Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
5,"Chatino, Zenzontepec",https://docs.verbix.com/Languages/ChatinoZenzontepec,"Zenzontepec Chatino, also known as Northern Chatino, or ""Chatino Occidental Alto"" is an indigenous Mesoamerican language, one of the Chatino family of the Oto-Manguean languages.","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
6,Ep. 39: Eric W. Campbell on Otomanguean Language Documentation...,https://lingfieldnotes.podbean.com/e/ep-39-eric-w-campbell-on-otomanguean-language-documentation-mobilization/,"Eric approaches language in its social and cultural context, focusing on less-studied languages, especially the Otomanguean languages spoken in Mexico and California. Things mentioned in this episode: Zapotec languages Purépecha language Chatino languages Zenzontepec...","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
7,Zenzontepec Chatino - czn (Otomanguean) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/czn/,"Zenzontepec Chatino (czn) is part of the Otomanguean family and Otomanguean, Eastern Otomanguean, Popolocan-Zapotecan, Zapotecan, Chatino class.","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
8,Tones in San Juan Quiahije Chatino,https://bpb-us-w2.wpmucdn.com/campuspress.yale.edu/dist/4/1207/files/2015/10/Cruz_SSMCA-12wxw2k.pdf,"Chatino forms a language subgroup that is coordinate with the Zapotecan language family within the Otomanguean linguistic stock (Kaufman 1993, Upson & Longacre 1965). There are three varieties of Chatino: Zenzontepec, Tataltepec and Eastern Chatino (Campbell 2013).","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
9,Documentation of Zenzontepec Chatino Language and Culture,https://www.elararchive.org/dk0185/,"English: Zenzontepec Chatino (ISO 639-3 czn), is referred to as tsá’ jnyá in the language itself. Chatino is a group of languages of the Zapotecan language family of the Otomanguean stock.","Chatino, Zenzontepec",Otomanguean
